    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0144" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5801</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs to the Chinese
                        Legation</hi><anchor n="57" xml:id="d37-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-09">January 9, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Marshal Chang Hsiao-Liang, in an interview given to Chinese and foreign
                    correspondents, declared: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Since international peace efforts appear to have ceased to be effective,
                            I see no way to maintain peace and protect China except through
                            sacrificing our lives and blood.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d37-f1" n="57" type="source" xml:id="d37-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram transmitted to the Department by the Chinese Legation on January
                    9.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
